751413400,flightphp,fleact,https://github.com/flightphp/fleact,3,1,2024-02-01T15:08:08Z,2025-09-26T05:49:57Z,JavaScript,flightphp/fleact,False,False,True,False,False,🚀 Quick and easy React starter template with a FlightPHP backend 💻🌐✨,main,https://faslatam.42web.io/fleact,0,Organization,flightphp,MIT,MIT License,1,2,3,False,False,composer-project; flight; php; react; starter-template; template-project; restful-application,0,,,,0,,9,False,,,,37,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,,,"Fleact is a quick and easy React starter template with a FlightPHP backend. This template allows you to kickstart web application development using React on the frontend and FlightPHP on the backend. 🚀 Start building your web projects swiftly and efficiently with React! 💻🌐✨

## Learn velt stack:

- [React](https://react.dev)
- [Flight](https://docs.flightphp.com)

## Requirements

- NodeJS >= 18
- PHP >= 7.4
- Composer >= 2

## Installation

### Using composer
```bash
composer create-project flightphp/fleact <my-project>
cd <my-project>
npm install
composer install
npm run dev
```

<!--
### With Flight CLI (coming soon...)
```bash
composer global require --dev flightphp/cli # or
npm install -g flight-cli

flight new <my-project> --react
```
-->

### Using git

Clone this repo running:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/flightphp/fleact <my-project>
cd <my-project>
npm install
composer install
npm run dev
```

If you don't want to keep git template history you can delete .git folder
```bash
rm .git -rf # linux/mac/windows git bash
RD /Q /S .git # windows
```

Or you can skip all this and use next method 👇🏽

### Using degit
```bash
npx degit flightphp/fleact <my-project>
cd <my-project>
npm install
composer install
npm run dev
```

