470727791,DenisSoloveyDev,webpack-kit__vanila-multipage-figma-plugin,https://github.com/DenisSoloveyDev/webpack-kit__vanila-multipage-figma-plugin,5,0,2022-03-16T19:39:56Z,2025-10-03T13:56:06Z,JavaScript,DenisSoloveyDev/webpack-kit__vanila-multipage-figma-plugin,False,False,True,False,False,"An easily customizable, multifunctional template for figma plugin development with file structure and atomic component generators. Simple configuration via JSON without editing Webpack configs. Supports Pug, EJS, HTML, SCSS/SASS, CSS, TS, JS. Production build mode includes resource optimization, as well as optional minification, hashing, and ZIP",main,,0,User,DenisSoloveyDev,,,0,0,5,True,False,webpack; figma; figma-plugins; pug; js; javascript; sass; vanilla-javascript; vanilla-js; eslint; stylelint; linter; html; css; bundle; atomic-design,0,,,,0,,9,False,,,,28,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,,,"### [ EN | [RU](https://github.com/DenisSoloveyDev/webpack-kit-vanila-multipage-figma-plugin/blob/main/README.ru.md) ]

# Webpack Kit - Vanila Multipage Figma Plugin

[![node][node]][node-url]

Easily customizable multi-functional template for *Figma plugins development* with generation of file structure, atomic components, and multipage support from box.

## Table of Contents

- [Quick start](#Quick-start)
- [Introduction](#Introduction)
- [Console commands](#Console-commands)
- [Settings of project.config.json](#Settings-of-projectconfigjson)
- [Settings of webpack.config.json](#Settings-of-webpackconfigjson)
- [Pre-installed packages](#Pre-installed-packages)
  - [For development](#For-development)
  - [For functioning of bundler](#For-functioning-of-bundler)

## Quick Start

Installation of packages:

```bash
npm i
```

Start-up generation of project structure:

```bash
npm run project
```

The launch in development mode on dev-server:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The launch of production-build:

```bash
npm run build
```

## Introduction

Webpack 5 based template is intended for quick start in Figma plugin development. Provides flexible configuration without the need for manual editing of webpack configs. Supports work with multiple pages.

It includes additionally a self-written scripts: 

- to start the project structure generation,
- to create atomic components by one console comand.

Supports the work with prepocessors: `Pug` (with extended `pugbem` plugin supporting custom prefixes for simplified work on BEM), `EJS`, `SCSS`, `SASS`, `TypeScript`. Also works with vanilla `HTML`, `CSS` and `JavaScript`.


Production-build includes optimization of the assets, as well as optional minimization and ZIP-archiving.

### Features

- **Support of multi-page development** 
<br>No need to create HtmlWebpackPlugin instances for each page manually. Just add pages to the directory and you can start working.
- **Project generation** 
<br>The kit contains self-written script to generate the source files structure. It generates the required files based on parameters set in `project.config.json`, using pre-prepared templates.
- **Generator of components** 
<br>Quick creation of atoms/molecules/organisms for selected preprocessors by one team.
- **Easy switching between preprocessors at start**
<br>Simply specify the necessary extensions in `project.config.json`, generate the project and you can start developing.
- **Webpack configuration via JSON** 
<br>No need to manually edit the webpack. All the key parameters - entry points, connection of scripts to pages, hosting, minimization etc. - are configured via `webpack.config.json`.
- **Rich collection of libraries** 
<br>The template includes both popular and less common, but useful libraries and plugins for development.

## Console commands

Webpack modes:

```shell 
npm run dev    # development mode
npm run debug  # debug mode
npm run build  # production-build
npm run build --min # production-build with minimization
```

Project generation:

```shell 
npm run project
```

Component generation:

```shell 
npm run create --atom <component-name> +js # Create component in atoms folder
npm run create --mol  <component-name> +js # Create a component in the molecules folder
npm run create --org  <component-name> +js # Create component in organisms folder
```

\*_`+js` — optional parameter that tells the generator whether to create a script file for the component._

## Settings of project.config.json

#### `plugin-name` | `String`

The name of the plugin that will be specified in the manifest.

---

#### `include-ui` | `Boolean`

Turns on/off the creation of a plugin UI structure for webpack to work with. If disabled, `""npm run create""` will not work.

---

#### `enable-atomic-design` | `Boolean`

Turns on/off the creation of a atomic design structure. If disabled, `""npm run create""` will not work.

---

#### `camelCase` | `Boolean`

Converts the names of classes, mixins, functions etc. to camelCase format.

---

#### `include-gitkeep` | `Boolean`

Parameter responsible for creating a special file inside empty folders, so that they can be thrown into the repository.

---

#### `templates-src` | `String` or `null`

Relative path to the folder with personalized templates, for example `""./custom-templates-folder/template-folder""`. If the value is empty, default templates are used.

---

#### `types.<type>` | `String`

Values:
<br>`types.template` &emsp; –&emsp; `""pug""`, `""ejs""`, `""html""`
<br>`types.style` &nbsp;&ensp;&emsp;&emsp;–&emsp; `""scss""`, `""sass""`, `""css""`
<br>`types.script` &nbsp;&emsp;&emsp;–&emsp; `""ts""`, `""js""`

Extension with which files will be created and which specifies the preprocessor to work with.

---

#### `editor` | `String` or `null`

Values: `""code""`, `""sublime""`, `""atom""`, `""webstorm""`, `""phpstorm""`, `""idea14ce""`, `""vim""`, `""emacs""`, `""visualstudio""`

The editor in which the created atomic component files will be opened.

---

#### `editor-path` | `String` or `null`

Absolute path to the .exe editor file in which created atomic component files will be opened, for example `""C:/Program Files/Microsoft VS Code/Code.exe""`

---

#### `source-name` | `String` <br>`<param>.source-name` | `String` or `null`

The name of the root folder or sectiom in the source folder. Created by the project generator and used by Webpack. If the name value of the folder for the section is empty, then the files processed by the collector will be merged in the root.

project.config.json
```JSON
  ""source-name"": ""app"", # Name of the root folder
 
  ""API"": {
    ""source-name"": """", # Name of section in the root
    ""create"": [""folder1/"", ""folder2/file1""]
  },
```
File structure 
```bash
|-- app
  |-- folder1
  |-- folder2
    |-- file1
```

---

#### `build-name` | `String`

The name of the root folder. If the value is empty, the scripts will not work.

---

#### `create` | `String[]` or `null`

An array of subsections and files that will be created by the generator within a section, for example `[""folder/file"", ""folder/"", ""file""]`.
<br> There is no need to write the file extension.

---

#### `template-set` | `String` or `Boolean`

Values: `""all""`, `""by-name""`, `""only-index""`, `false`

Specifies how to paste the content of templates into files which were specified in `create`, and `index`:
<br>`""all""` - The content of the `index` template is inserted into all files
<br>`""by-name""` - The contents of a template are inserted into a file if their names match
<br>`""only-index""` - Template content is inserted into `index` only
<br>`false` - Templates do not apply

---

#### `inject-head` | `Boolean`

Specifies how to paste the content of the `head` template into the page files. If `false` — `head` will be taken out by a separate component and connected via `include`. Does not work with vanilla `HTML`.

---

#### `inject` | `Boolean`

Insert the contents of files that were specified in `create` into `index`. If `false` — separate files will be created and connected via imports.

---

#### `name` | `String`

The name of the section of atomic names or their root folder. Must not be empty, otherwise the scripts `npm run project` and `npm run create` will not work.

---

#### `prefix` | `String` or `null`

Prefix for the name of atomic components. If the value is empty, the prefix will not apply.

---

#### `set-types.<type>` | `Boolean`

File with extension of specified type, which should be generated when the specified components are created in  `create` and import to which will be inserted into corresponding `index`. Does not apply to `npm run create`.

webpack.config.json
```JSON
""types"": { ""template"": ""pug"", ""style"": ""scss"", ""script"": ""ts"" },

""atomic-design"": {
  ""atoms"": {
    ""create"": [""a"", ""b""],
    ""set-type"": {
      ""template"": true,
      ""style"": false,
      ""script"": true
    }
  }
},
```
File structure
```bash
|-- atoms
  |-- a-a
    |-- a-a.pug
    |-- a-a.ts
  |-- a-b
    |-- a-b.pug
    |-- a-b.ts
```


## Settings of webpack.config.json

#### `entries.<chunk>` | `String`

`Key` — the name of the entry point, `value` — the path/file name without extension (relative to the root folder of the source files or section, depending on `project.config.json`).

Declares scripts as entry points for compilation. Only works with string values.

`index` is a required value. It must specify the relative path to the file from which the plugin works.

---

#### `provide-plugins.<plugin>` | `String`

Global identifiers that are pulled in via `ProvidePlugin`. Allows libraries to be used without imports in every file. See the [webpack documentation](https://webpack.js.org/plugins/provide-plugin/) for details.

---

#### `chunks-to-page.<chunk>` | `String[]`

`Key` - the page name, `value` - the array of script names to connect.

Connecting scripts specified in `entries`,  to HTML pages. The script name must match the key name in `entries`.


- Special key `all-pages` - apply the specified chunks to all pages.

---

#### `pugbem.<prefix>` | `String`

Configuration of the `pugbem` extension for convenient working with BEM-syntax in Pug.

webpack.config.json
```JSON
""pugbem"": {
  ""input-modificator"": ""--"",
  ""input-element"": ""__"",
  ""output-modificator"": ""**"",
  ""output-element"": ""++""
},
```
Pug
```Pug
.parent
  .__child.--mod
```
HTML
```HTML
<div class=""parent"">
  <div class=""parent++child parent++child**mod""></div>
</div>
```

---

#### `minify` | `Boolean`

Includes JS/CSS minimization and JS obfuscation during production-build. Also, you can enable minimization by adding `--min` to the `npm run build` comand.

---

#### `source-maps` | `Boolean`

Generation of sourcemap files during production-build.

---

#### `zip` | `Boolean`

Archiving the results of production-bundle in a separate ZIP.


## Pre-installed packages

### For Development

- [@create-figma-plugin/utilities](https://yuanqing.github.io/create-figma-plugin/utilities/) – Library of utility functions for common Figma/FigJam plugin/widget operations.
- [@figma-plugin/helpers](https://github.com/figma-plugin-helper-functions/figma-plugin-helpers) – A collection of useful helper functions.
- [barba.js](https://barba.js.org/) – Animated page transitions.
- [fancybox](https://fancyapps.com/fancybox/) – Modals, galleries and lightboxes for images, videos and HTML-content.
- [gsap](https://gsap.com/) – A powerful and widely used JavaScript-library for creating high-performance web animations at different levels.
- [jquery](https://jquery.com/) – Easy to use(work) with DOM, events and AJAX.
- [swiper](https://swiperjs.com/) – Modern adaptive-touch slider with multiple effects.
- [three.js](https://threejs.org/) – Work with WebGL and 3D graphics: scenes, cameras, materials, models.
- [d3](https://d3js.org/) – Powerful library for data visualization and work with graphics.
- [animejs](https://animejs.com/) – Universal animation library for DOM, SVG, CSS and JavaScript-objects.
- [apexCharts](https://apexcharts.com/) – Interactive graphics and diagrams for the Web with rich settings.
- [apexGrids](https://apexcharts.com/apexgrid/) – ApexCharts extension to display tables with data.
- [apexGantt](https://apexcharts.com/apexgantt/) – Gantt diagram based on ApexCharts for task planning.
- [apexStock](https://apexcharts.com/apexstock/) – Components for stock market and financial data visualization.
- [apexTree](https://apexcharts.com/apextree/) – Tree diagrams to display hierarchies.
- [apexSankey](https://apexcharts.com/apexsankey/) – Sankey diagrams for visualizing flows and distributions.
- [autocomplete.js](https://tarekraafat.github.io/autoComplete.js/#/) – Easy autocompile for text fields with customizable data sources.
- [infinite-ajax-scroll](https://infiniteajaxscroll.com/) – Endless scrolling and uploading of content without rebooting the page.
- [air-datepicker](https://air-datepicker.com/) – Compact and customizable calendar/datepicker.
- [animatedScrollTo-js](https://gist.github.com/gangsthub/0bce1161cfd2aa91ae7cad9abb42c342) – Smooth animated scrolling to page elements.
- [binking](https://github.com/svagcrew/binking) – Takes the bank’s logo, colors, name etc. depending on the card number entered.
- [choices.js](https://choices-js.github.io/Choices/) – Custom select, input and tags with search and multiple choice.
- [data-ripple](https://github.com/mopcweb/data-ripple) – Adds ""ripple"" effect for clickable elements.
- [dynamics.js](https://github.com/michaelvillar/dynamics.js?ref=vanillalist) – Spring curve for animations.
- [imask](https://imask.js.org/) – Flexible input masks for text fields (phone, map, date, etc.).
