160745599,adobe,aio-cli-plugin-boilerplate,https://github.com/adobe/aio-cli-plugin-boilerplate,6,7,2018-12-06T23:32:47Z,2025-04-04T03:45:08Z,JavaScript,adobe/aio-cli-plugin-boilerplate,False,False,True,False,False,Basic working repo structure for Adobe teams to use as a starting point for their own plugins.,main,,0,Organization,adobe,Apache-2.0,Apache License 2.0,7,12,6,True,False,adobe-io; adobe-io-cli; adobe; adobe-io-cli-plugin; cli,0,,,,0,,9,False,,,,87,True,True,True,contributor_covenant,False,True,True,False,,,"# aio-cli-plugin-boilerplate

Basic working repo structure for Adobe teams to use as a starting point for their own plugins, and available as a github template to the @adobe github org.

## How to use this template

- create a new repo from the github.com/adobe and select it in the templates
- give it a unique name ( plugins are typically named aio-cli-plugin-xxxx )
- enter a description
- pick options
- create repository
- `git clone`, `npm i`
- make some changes to names of things readme, ...
- `git add .`
- `git commit -m 'A new begining'`

## How to use this repo, ( like a repo )

- Click 'Clone or Download' and download a zip
- extract it to a directory on your machine
- if you cloned, delete the hidden `.git` folder
- run `git init`
- make some changes to names of things readme, ...
- `git add .`
- `git commit -m 'A new begining'`

- Create the new empty repo here on github
- grab the remote url 

### back in your directory ...

- `git remote add origin new-repo-url`
- `git push origin master`

